the directory instead of preventing unrelated planned changes from being restored.\\n\\n\\u003ca href=\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fsystem%2Fhistory%2Freplay.rs%0ALine%3A%201010-1011%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Unreadable%20Directory%20Aborts%20Rollback**%0A%0AIf%20an%20otherwise%20disposable%20directory%20contains%20an%20unreadable%20descendant%2C%20this%20scan%20propagates%20the%20traversal%20error%20and%20aborts%20the%20entire%20rollback%20or%20undo.%20The%20normal%20history%20walker%20records%20unreadable%20paths%20as%20omitted%20and%20continues%2C%20while%20this%20scan%20only%20decides%20whet\",\"comment\":3945285524,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFHf\",\"pr\":12835}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Unreadable Directory Aborts Rollback**\\n\\nIf an otherwise disposable directory contains an unreadable descendant, this scan propagates the traversal error and aborts the entire rollback or undo. The normal history walker records unreadable paths as omitted and continues, while this scan only decides whether an optional directory-cleanup step is safe. An inspection failure should therefore preserve the directory instead of preventing unrelated planned changes from being restored.\\n\\n\\u003ca href=\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fsystem%2Fhistory%2Freplay.rs%0ALine%3A%201010-1011%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Unreadable%20Directory%20Aborts%20Rollback**%0A%0AIf%20an%20otherwise%20disposable%20directory%20contains%20an%20unreadable%20descendant%2C%20this%20scan%20propagates%20the%20traversal%20error%20and%20aborts%20the%20entire%20rollback%20or%20undo.%20The%20normal%20history%20walker%20records%20unrea