{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T21:53:23.364Z","ordinal":9033,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de0b5d99887d0b0754ee3014e604a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_mdDHSnKQmihzfvWfFHppTOL2","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\\n@@\\n # Dotfiles stack takeover\\n+\\n+## IN PROGRESS heartbeat September 6 21:43 UTC: main rebase and three new fixes\\n+\\n+No pushes or GitHub replies yet in this heartbeat. Expected remote heads are the six in the completed push below (a04a62048/dbb901d75/3edad6aa8/3b00de37e/7a9037390/5cb5808). Verified unchanged at start. Main advanced to b396c62bc (CLI reference rewrite #12885); foundation conflicted and prevented normal PR test workflows, only review/title checks ran on prior push. Never claim last pushed heads passed full CI.\\n+\\n+Foundation rebased onto b396c62bc and committed regenerated docs in 3f967b880. Preserved new main bootstrap help, merged dotfile status help, and kept new cli-reference.ts generator/tests in tasks.toml alongside optional-subcommand normalization. Generated-file conflicts selected ours and were fully regenerated afterwards. Foundation full render/lint-fix + track_experimental E2E PASS; clean.\\n+Rollback rebased onto foundation, new head19b1756b5 (includes regenerated reference). New fix originally aec7d03a2, now5399cb731: optional directory cleanup treats unreadable-descendant inspection as reason to preserve directory, not abort whole rollback. Regression adds chmod000 child and verifies neighbor deletion + child preservation. E2E54105 PASS; rebased full render/lint32515 PASS; clean.\\n+Services rebased onto rollback, headbd9e4196e before generated docs commit. Resolved source bootstrap help: retain new concise phase order, add user services and post-tool service phase; retain cross-platform services help. Full render/lint session22217 RUNNING. Must poll, review generated diff, commit, then restack watcher.\\n+Watcher still OLD current3b00de37e, not yet rebased; rebase onto services using old base3edad6aa8, resolve docs, render/lint/commit.\\n+Origin still based on old watcher; own new commit5508f8073 rejects empty variant names and `/`/`@` separators. New cross-platform variant round-trip unit PASS (14914), lint-fix PASS. Rebase onto new watcher using old base3b00de37e after ready, render/lint.\\n+Auto still based on old origin; own new commit3d148c7b4 reuses held purge lock for disconnect and acquires lock before standalone remove rewrites config. New helper remove_locked uses run::SyncStatus. Added purge regression to test_dotfiles_sync_permissions: delete this-machine recovery refs, disconnected status, shared main remains. Initial lint44102 failed wrong type module, fixed; final lint+E2E7957 PASS. Rebase onto new origin using old base7a9037390 when ready, render/lint and focused integrated tests.\\n+\\n+Only ACTIVE terminal session at this note: 22217 services render then lint. Other sessions complete. Nothing touched encryption/blog/original141d. All changes scoped existing worktrees/branches. Finish restack, verify expected heads, atomic lease push all six, inspect actual CI, reply/resolve these new findings with evidence: rollback3945285524 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFHf; origin3945310321 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLR; auto3945294364 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvGkw.\\n+\\n+New remaining reviews (in addition to old queue below): #12865 this-machine name/ref uses fetched backups rather than local checkpoints3945289138 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn; incoming unknown policy keys silently default share3945310318 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ; embedded credential URL rejection3945310329 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV (duplicates older credential leakage); bootstrap_completed missing lock on #9 3945310331 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX (#10 already holds lock, consider moving earlier). #12849 and #12838/#12843 had no unresolved threads at start. No new substantive CI failure logs because normal tests weren't dispatched while root PR conflicted.\\n+\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","create_time":1788731569.131257}}}
