{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:06:12.408Z","ordinal":9349,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","session_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","root_turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de346342c87d084d9db418ffc1549","usage":{"input_tokens":228845,"cached_input_tokens":222080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4642,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":233487},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":17713104,"cached_input_tokens":17583232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24884,"reasoning_output_tokens":4770,"total_tokens":17737988},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":164737542,"cached_input_tokens":160804864,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":438372,"reasoning_output_tokens":83944,"total_tokens":165175914}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:06:12.417Z","type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de346342c87d084d9db418ffc1549","first_window_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4aa0d35d1afe","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"i'm thinking like `mise history paths add ~/.zshrc --platform macos-arm64`? what do you think?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071c8-1801-7593-a4d0-89c2c045fccd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615333.889248,"turn_id":"01a071c8-174e-74c0-856f-1462026e1554"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we have some prior art with things like mise.macos.toml\n\nbut how would this work under the hood? would I still be able to edit \\~/.zshrc and have it autosync just for macs?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071c8-d7a1-7850-8ef9-ecc5e4376ae1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615382.945137,"turn_id":"01a071c8-d6ec-7a22-9248-ed12d9595e3d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think users would prefer if the platform was inside the same config file\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071c9-b133-76a1-9e2f-7a7a90466ef6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615438.643792,"turn_id":"01a071c9-b080-7bb2-bac3-8b66bba68168"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok does that model work for other chezmoi gaps?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071c9-fbd7-7e62-9d26-5691c7d44d00","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615457.75196,"turn_id":"01a071c9-fb24-71b0-b932-2285a9e7ae62"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: `mise history` — automatic configuration history (single authoritative …\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/313b84f6-06c6-46ce-bcd9-b0ed8d2ae348/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nok here's the latest draft, tell me how to improve it based on what we discussed since: \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ca-d9c6-71a2-8f39-cb9611775af5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615514.56633,"turn_id":"01a071ca-d910-7070-9681-36c16f7b21fd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what does backup encrypted and share false do?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071cc-97fc-7a43-8fcc-9d51650216d2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615628.796985,"turn_id":"01a071cc-9751-70c0-a1d9-3c6a46adc9d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how do those work under the hood?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071cc-fe02-7581-bb30-c9ae4e64192b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615654.9148,"turn_id":"01a071cc-fd3e-7ac1-b722-16bcfffc634d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think another useful config would be for noisy files, like i might want to share a file but not have it automatically persist\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071cd-d37d-7680-8c34-56c0d7892ea3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615709.565342,"turn_id":"01a071cd-d2bd-78c2-be5f-d851021fe664"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think another thing we should account for is having something like templates. I was thinking we already solve that with bootstrap dotfiles so we probably just need to make sure they can use both of them together\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ce-9f51-7130-9074-952fae50a84b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615761.745528,"turn_id":"01a071ce-9e9b-7313-b43a-4c5904bee6a5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok how does this plan compare to chezmoi then? also, users will want the templates and the history stuff to be in the same git repo, how will that work?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071cf-400f-7d30-a80f-5608f920ba38","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615802.895281,"turn_id":"01a071cf-3f50-7181-b623-451d8dba0a07"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: `mise history` — automatic configuration history with sync (single auth…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/1e482590-f4d5-4b5a-8148-73194a87903c/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nhere's the latest revision, tell me what to modify, I think it missed some of the stuff we talked about \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d0-0e4b-70d1-bc2d-e08cbf8e6634","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788615855.691127,"turn_id":"01a071d0-0d83-7a83-8305-ee35df4436f5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i am kind of wondering if we should flatten this into bootstrap.dotfiles\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d4-0486-7e23-a8de-fc5403266ed5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616115.334975,"turn_id":"01a071d4-03b1-7760-96ca-f6c4a1c91553"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i don't understand, doesn't that example config conflict with the current dotfiles setup?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d4-e7d4-77e0-a9fe-ff851e8ebfa7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616173.524847,"turn_id":"01a071d4-e72e-7e51-bd7e-0f6405122cf5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we should restructure the docs too because we'll want them to use tracking since it's the better way to manage the dotfiles. we should provide a golden path setup for bootstrap (btw the bootstrap docs might need to be restructred and cleaned up anyhow) but the golden path should be tracked config files, setting up the origin and all that. I think the current setup is useful as an alternative or fallback for things like templating\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d6-8039-7e01-805a-fd9a5ccf2a81","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616278.073427,"turn_id":"01a071d6-7f6f-7501-8bc6-30f5a7dc353f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think you should read the current bootstrap docs and see how best to merge it with this concept\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d7-2a54-7f13-a431-de843b38d2b7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616321.620509,"turn_id":"01a071d7-2997-7a62-9b2a-54ff35d7f92e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"could we have separate docs per os? or perhaps maybe some examples that show things like omarchy, ubuntu, macos, and windows? we could have cookbooks too but i think those are a bit hidden but we could link to them for more esoteric setups\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d8-b36d-7282-8299-642f63a94ac7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616422.253996,"turn_id":"01a071d8-b2a7-7eb2-9259-f2370fc52296"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: `mise history` — configuration history, sharing, and setup (single auth…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/f8b2dcb1-fa5a-4d4c-af9e-6444dbeda97f/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nok based on what we discussed since the last review, tell me how to modify the latest plan \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071d9-c908-7ea2-a406-074e1eb2f50f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616493.320486,"turn_id":"01a071d9-c833-7b91-a564-4f5be771061c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"in \\~/src/blog, write a blog post assuming we launched this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071db-b323-73f0-a488-76931e79ed6c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788616618.78736,"turn_id":"01a071db-b26b-71f2-b554-a82f19ce88d5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: bootstrap adopts and recreates your setup; `[dotfiles]` declares how ea…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/876266e9-46aa-4d5b-8150-6dd8e9abd323/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nhow does this plan look now \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e2-028e-73c2-b637-226702d0de02","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617032.334099,"turn_id":"01a071e2-0179-70d2-aa7a-311127da97c2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i like the idea of `watch = t`rue but i think it should live in bootstrap.services instead unless you disagree\n\n\n\n### 2. Fetch must not update the active global configuration\n\nwhy not? i'm not so sure\n\n\n\nI think we should prevent users from adding .local.toml files but maybe give them a setting to opt out of that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e4-fff9-7881-9841-88892fd08602","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617228.281127,"turn_id":"01a071e4-ff34-7bd2-ae86-91db6458b725"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do we not support user-level services too? i thought we did, if not, that'll be a prereq for this stack\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e5-e132-7dc3-82ca-35bf3c5d23f1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617285.938672,"turn_id":"01a071e5-e073-7e51-84f3-4251db875b92"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"mise bootstrap history apply\n\nmise history status\n\n- that is weird\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e6-5822-70d3-b566-9940368fa241","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617316.386237,"turn_id":"01a071e6-5760-7e43-a848-f4932ed38b4a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me the instructions to send back to the other agent\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e7-1007-7f00-b86a-2b098b1c9789","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617363.463932,"turn_id":"01a071e7-0f51-79e1-bee8-84b9d98d9cd7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"also update your blog post\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071e8-000a-73d1-b6ab-8ca2a501ee05","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617424.906856,"turn_id":"01a071e7-ff64-7801-a774-8ced7e53c96b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think in the blog post we can explicitly call out tools like chezmoi as an example and where it falls flat, but also be honest if there are gaps with mise\n\nsecrets may be one, but we also have secrets in env and fnox so it is less important\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071eb-4d87-7651-9468-b72f45874c4d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617641.351204,"turn_id":"01a071eb-4cc5-7242-83fb-345f82178664"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"mise is never capitalized btw\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ec-969a-7850-b12a-4cc673ba1d36","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617725.59467,"turn_id":"01a071ec-95f2-7d10-b9a1-8458f6016ae7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i used to use a dotfile manager called rcm, maybe worth showing my former workflow in the intro. i had this `git-sync.sh` thing that I manually installed as a launchagent, you might be able to find jdx/dotfiles-old or something with it\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ef-4e26-7b62-a9c6-9db3a0c9ba59","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788617903.654426,"turn_id":"01a071ef-4c3e-76e1-8c2b-8eb6a20e5b23"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"that is not a public repo\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f1-fe09-7c21-af08-a3fa8298bd79","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618079.753048,"turn_id":"01a071f1-fbf7-72f3-9457-0a3df2c9aea2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the rcm involved a lot of custom flaky code and complex cli commands, it was a pain to onboard new boxes too. mise not only simplifies that but it has much more capability\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f3-9fac-7e90-adb8-a1d6d0c90799","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618186.668571,"turn_id":"01a071f3-9e5a-7b40-829a-5323e4ea8a06"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should hit on integrating with mise bootstrap so setup is just `mise bootstrap --from-git`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f4-3df7-7401-9336-f2dc79df2e7e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618227.191596,"turn_id":"01a071f4-3d2d-72b3-a014-63717c451580"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"saying that though, it's not enough since my dotfiles repo will be private. so there will be some initial setup like installing mise and setting up git auth before i can use it, could we improve that workflow with mise?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f5-0f90-74d0-9392-e18a23ceeb1b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618280.848926,"turn_id":"01a071f5-0db4-7ea2-994a-15e681b94e59"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"maybe read through my past blog posts to make this sound like i am writing it too\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f6-19b8-7f42-ab51-851bfd4da8f0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618348.98467,"turn_id":"01a071f6-18da-7f53-bc17-3250d9acf58a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i like your suggestion about --from-git improvements, let's include that in the plan, but before that, but before that maybe we could think about the current GITHUB\\_TOKEN setup stuff? we have a lot of ways to configure that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fa-b84e-7693-a40f-59aa242f4866","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618651.726768,"turn_id":"01a071fa-b793-75c2-bc53-4642c3e2b72c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"personally i would probably want to go with the oauth thing\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fc-a14e-7be2-a960-32a74231b812","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618776.910471,"turn_id":"01a071fc-a0a0-7a12-a1de-868a787d0155"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think this could go into the blog post, and maybe as a callout tip for the docs but generally the oauth app would be optinoal, i think users would need to setup gh and auth themselves—which they can install with mise\n\nso i think `curl mise.run, mise x gh -- gh auth login`, mise bootstrap --form-git\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fd-eacd-77b2-a1eb-996733f54563","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618861.261747,"turn_id":"01a071fd-ea15-7f61-9f79-0ac7634d9740"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"or alternatively we should have a workflow for mise bootstrap remote, ideally where we can somehow share the token with the remote box. i think what would be really cool in fact is if we didn't need to put the token on the box and instead could use the host as a proxy to talk to github\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ff-131b-7030-a3f5-4aed4285648b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618937.115176,"turn_id":"01a071ff-1268-79a3-b250-d5a95b9d1692"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: bootstrap adopts and recreates the setup; `[dotfiles]` declares file ma…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/e48b166e-161b-49a3-9d17-7c4072d06ac9/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nneat idea, i have another agent working on it now.\n\nNow, take what we've discussed and review the latest plan draft\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07200-d4aa-7252-aab7-90aeccdc0f63","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619052.202824,"turn_id":"01a07200-d3e2-7901-8d8b-e0fffa61dcaa"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"question, when they use --from-git does it get stored as a bare repo?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07207-6c07-7342-9df1-c086bb20cdf9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619484.167703,"turn_id":"01a07207-6b43-72c0-a2b7-71529f2f0bb9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yeah let's simplify it, but we need backwards compat\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07207-c328-7b83-9438-5736c71705a7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619506.47214,"turn_id":"01a07207-c277-7cf0-868b-80483eded2c5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok but if they use a bare repo, how are they able to use something like templates?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07208-c193-7081-aa2c-0c30e99f4555","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619571.603653,"turn_id":"01a07208-c0e2-7981-a1e4-ab12890522e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"so they'd also probably need to track the templates?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07209-8758-7ef0-8ce5-8e0bb8b4222a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619622.23257,"turn_id":"01a07209-86a7-7c53-a49e-001dab1bbb3c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"agreed. so it sounds like if they want tracking they need to use bare\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720a-4590-7d82-9574-2f1099450607","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619670.928459,"turn_id":"01a0720a-44d0-7003-8d68-d8852a3fac33"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"show me some exapmles\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720a-c7a8-7d42-b948-61e9c91a705c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619704.232919,"turn_id":"01a0720a-c6f7-77d2-87a3-e0724fdc0290"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"oh so it's fine because we never actually managed the git repo before\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720b-ec41-7333-a87a-409cfd0f93c7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619779.137851,"turn_id":"01a0720b-eb8c-7750-b552-2024a1f14171"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me the full instructions to send to the other agent including your last corrections\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720c-2f47-7d83-825e-8341cf0b303b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619796.295168,"turn_id":"01a0720c-2e95-7741-8779-12b0e88a3d29"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: bootstrap adopts and recreates the setup; `[dotfiles]` declares file ma…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/e4d99c20-8c58-438f-8ec9-d7f84685c0a4/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nreview \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0721e-1748-71d1-88e8-d50fb16b2706","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788620969.800992,"turn_id":"01a0721e-1689-77a2-900c-63c2c3b82ba8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"make a pr for that blog post\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072e7-edfa-7c20-a213-ad4942c9ef99","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788634197.498089,"turn_id":"01a072e7-ec26-7300-9c9a-a4025ab5295a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"rebase the blog pr\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072e8-0e8f-7411-ac1d-f697e67f25ac","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788634205.839443,"turn_id":"01a072e7-ec26-7300-9c9a-a4025ab5295a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i believe all the prs are up, how does it look? how does it compare to the blog post?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07307-f793-7242-ae30-ac6e498dc712","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788636297.107288,"turn_id":"01a07307-f67e-7aa2-a103-fc48da7a7417"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if it should be `mise history` or `mise bootstrap history`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07348-9d82-72d0-8f35-1cb7fc6eeba4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788640533.890321,"turn_id":"01a07348-9c97-7dc1-be2a-a4ddbb3f55b4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"on the blog post\n\nI think we're explaining too much about rcm details\n\n\"and the part I'm most excited about is the integration with `mise bootstrap`\" it is part of mise bootstrap so that sounds weird\n\nsee the pr i landed with `mise ssh`, we should incorporate that into the blog post and later the pr stack\n\"private, btw,\" - remove the \"btw\"\n\n\"mise installs and runs `gh`, so you don't need to install it separately\" - obviously, but we should use the proxy thing from the mise ssh thing anyhow\n\nwe should show output for commands like \"mise bootstrap\"\n\n\"If the watcher isn't running, mise warns you and tells you how to set it up. Adding a file saves its current contents, but obviously it can't keep saving changes without something watching it.\" i think we can strike this\u0026#x20;\n\n\"After a short pause,\" how does the debouncing work exactly? I think it should be fairly complex, like save reasonably quick after a change unless the same file keeps beign modified or something, like have some sort of backoff? it's probably also worth explaining what happens if the user adds a noisy file (which we should tell them not to)\n\n\"Files ending in `.local.toml`, including mise's `config.local.toml`, are protected from sharing by default—even when you enroll their parent directory. They can still have local recovery history, and their remote backups follow the backup and encryption policies. If you deliberately want to share one, you can explicitly override that protection for the file.\" remove that\n\n\"Connecting an existing repository also checks outgoing history for private files that were already committed. Adding an ignore rule today doesn't make yesterday's commit private.\" - remove\n\n\nremove the section on chezmoi\n\nmake the section about secrets a lot shorter\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0736d-6ba9-7e13-82fc-05caacbd1e75","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788642945.961264,"turn_id":"01a0736d-6a8a-7773-ac4f-584d4500af7b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"that seems way too short, also, how does warning actually work when it's running as a service?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07370-910b-7893-937d-d50a3e131571","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643152.139706,"turn_id":"01a07370-903b-76b1-a7da-36cec20f393b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think it should go up to like 24 hours if the file continuously changes\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07371-0ac0-7552-95e3-3bf1285f28b5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643183.296302,"turn_id":"01a07371-09f5-7f72-86c0-729423541b84"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok edit the blog post to mention this, it doesn't need a lot of detail, i'll later have you instruct the other agent about this decision\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07371-7c12-7bd3-b45e-b6def9c1541e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643212.306618,"turn_id":"01a07371-7b50-7cb0-8378-37b5ea3403a7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the first time we mention mise bootstrap we should link to it\n\nI don't think we should use `mise ssh`, we should use `mise bootstrap remote` with the right flags for the github proxy\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07372-cf65-73e2-a6c3-0b98f9bd637a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643299.173311,"turn_id":"01a07372-ce80-7131-b302-8e2a3827cff0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"make this non-draft\n\nuse 'jdx/dotfiles' as my repo name\n\nwhat happens when there is a conflict when the service is running?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07376-2f97-7b22-ac73-2ed539030471","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643520.40775,"turn_id":"01a07376-2ed7-7143-a8f1-03f0b1614350"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The GitHub token stays on my laptop, and borrowed access ends when the bootstrap run finishes. This currently works between Linux and macOS machines. It’s read-only setup access, not permanent sync authentication: a remote machine that should push its own changes later still needs write credentials.\n\nmention after this `mise ssh` can be used for permanent sessions\n\n\"plus mise-managed recovery history for individual machines\" - is this sent to the origin repo?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07379-41fe-7fe0-b71c-839b946bd250","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643721.726146,"turn_id":"01a07379-412a-7d53-87cc-3ca28df3adc5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\"You don’t need a second repository just for templates.\" - this doesn't need to be said\n\nthe `mise ssh` thing can go into a tip callout\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737b-7694-7e71-a607-62291e84c951","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643866.260493,"turn_id":"01a0737b-75b6-7e22-abea-31c6e80a0c3c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if we conflated dotfile history with history of bootstrap apply things like installing packages\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737c-6f99-7db2-9c78-59b7ccfc5c67","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643930.009396,"turn_id":"01a0737c-6eda-7ef0-b918-3fd62ff6eedf"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"not really sure `mise history` makes sense, users would expect it to apply to things like `mise install` and `mise set`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737d-2404-7f53-b5b2-ce691eff326e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643976.196335,"turn_id":"01a0737d-2348-78f1-af8c-de230abba0f0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i also wonder if we should remove the journaling and stuff for non-file cahnges\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737d-99ac-7600-8238-70e1b92f03a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644006.316862,"turn_id":"01a0737d-98f2-77b2-aec3-5df661c0d2c9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"in that case I think it should all live inside `mise bootstrap` commands too\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737e-4869-73f1-b3a7-805b2e8ce6c2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644051.049767,"turn_id":"01a0737e-479d-7d91-8c4b-9744b093f8bf"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"give me some instructions for the agent about this and the mise ssh stuff since it's in progress\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737e-ac5a-7381-b563-806d9946f3ef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644076.634472,"turn_id":"01a0737e-ab89-7703-852e-bb746aaf852e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"also edit the blog post to reflect this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737f-764f-7fc0-8872-ae402cbf7c78","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644128.335156,"turn_id":"01a0737f-758c-7303-b0c9-9ac7f8e975b7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"## 5. Make background problems visible\n\nhow on earth are we going to achieve this?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-2d4d-7952-a113-2e16850f7f57","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644175.181632,"turn_id":"01a07380-2c90-76d0-be86-b438c1261a9e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we could use mise doctor\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-8245-7781-8c49-ed7ecae219c1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644196.933533,"turn_id":"01a07380-817a-7b90-af6a-34fcce586871"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me the full instructions again\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-b864-7951-bca3-aa19cd1ec001","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644210.788339,"turn_id":"01a07380-b791-71a2-83ed-8ee57a284a28"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Omarchy was a big motivation for this. I want users to keep editing their native config files, including having agents edit them, and have mise take care of the history and setup. You shouldn’t need to translate your configuration into another language to get that. This doesn’t automatically merge your customizations with distro updates though, or replace an OS snapshot.\n\n- remove that paragraph\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07387-6158-7343-ab81-76f1b5b86b8a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644647.256247,"turn_id":"01a07387-5f77-7743-b919-562cca7273b1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You can also select platform-specific variants. - we should show an example of this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07387-f4ef-7500-8697-8f60102eeec5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644685.039369,"turn_id":"01a07387-f429-78d1-8664-59cf1e17d782"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"These work together. The template source travels with the shared setup, and bootstrap renders it using the destination machine’s inputs. The generated `.gitconfig` isn’t shared as though it were the source.\n\nIf you edit the generated file, local history can help recover that edit, but the next render may replace it. mise doesn’t pretend it can reverse a rendered file back into a template.\n\nExisting symlink, copy, and managed-edit workflows still work. You don’t have to migrate a setup you’re happy with. There are also recipes for mixed-platform setups, templates, and moving an existing dotfiles repository to tracking.\n\n- that section is confusing to me\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07388-6f93-70b3-85b7-5eec9664a7ee","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644716.435732,"turn_id":"01a07388-6ed0-7e42-8a09-237a1f8c1fd6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok do that, then give the entire post a read through and make improvmeent suggestions\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07388-e96d-7573-aed4-dfe1fa1b6f98","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644747.629587,"turn_id":"01a07388-e8b4-7ce2-8345-dbf484d062a1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do all of that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07389-f0b6-7ad1-a9e5-72d9e5025dd5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644815.030702,"turn_id":"01a07389-efeb-74d0-b6b0-dcef9389f100"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"background history service ? remove that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738c-6062-71c2-939e-be54dcc65df8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644974.690759,"turn_id":"01a0738c-5faa-7b73-ab44-6d93a9f5ab50"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"This is file history, not a record of everything mise does. Bootstrap saves configuration before and after changing it, but restoring those files doesn’t reverse package installations or service state changes. Rolling back an `ffmpeg` declaration, for example, leaves the installed package alone.\n\n- no user would assume this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738d-e3a9-7b73-9778-e3dbf42b2a1f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645073.833476,"turn_id":"01a0738d-e2da-7bb2-ab0b-e929cc75866d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"maybe show the example config for configuring it with claude\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738e-5d9c-7453-8e9c-39e3dc2d5e1e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645105.05287,"turn_id":"01a0738e-5ce3-7082-8ce1-468c17181e11"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should have a setting for optional desktop notifications on sync conflicts\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738f-26c2-7b01-9970-17e8fe3cfe2c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645156.546013,"turn_id":"01a0738f-25fc-79b1-b737-08d74520d422"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"add that to the blog, just a brief mention\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738f-7aba-74e3-8645-37fe7d2735f9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645178.04221,"turn_id":"01a0738f-7a01-73a0-8185-1297a2de28b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"review the pr stack\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07400-afd5-7ec2-828e-f320ccbcf4bd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652597.205801,"turn_id":"01a07400-aea6-70a1-b6b4-e8a3bf84b419"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07402-1594-75d0-a304-f67339be4807","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652688.788864,"turn_id":"01a07402-14ca-7311-a89c-d39b9c2488bd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post the comments, including the gaps and alignment issues, why can't you use gh?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07402-d91a-7483-8e2d-cf9a836faa15","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652738.842006,"turn_id":"01a07402-d852-7043-8d30-4870c1fd9dca"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"were those the only ones that needed comments?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07405-8594-7531-bbbd-9a18551bc088","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652914.06827,"turn_id":"01a07405-84c6-7ac3-ab1a-d4bd9c5a8162"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok look at all of the prs\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07405-f418-7320-a0b8-cc9a2d132521","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652942.360742,"turn_id":"01a07405-f35d-7971-a9c9-4b757f525c8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0740a-f88b-7df1-b91b-56a2f910c3e5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788653271.179205,"turn_id":"01a0740a-f7bb-7c01-a437-621f4990b698"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how is the stack looking now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a074e9-f23c-7e41-9a86-ab42df6d83c3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788667884.092092,"turn_id":"01a074e9-f029-7b41-9d5b-15393cc141f0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a074ec-fc37-74c0-b8df-4d09b70172d5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788668083.255237,"turn_id":"01a074ec-fb3a-7160-80ce-1cf4ecb0fe8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"give it another pass, post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07545-ab74-7600-aeb9-346c3511708b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788673895.284972,"turn_id":"01a07545-a993-7112-87cf-c926ae1d5134"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"are there gaps?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07548-8155-7210-8ff5-0d860b19e3a8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788674081.109154,"turn_id":"01a07548-8077-7b63-a03f-e67f62bdd635"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me instructions for the agent to close the gaps\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07549-99af-79b3-b211-7642ae906637","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788674152.879463,"turn_id":"01a07549-98e7-7e42-b49a-91290a55dcd5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how does the stack look now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07744-b60c-7252-a02c-c727bdb84656","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707386.892536,"turn_id":"01a07744-b3c8-76e0-81d3-d3d855644ad2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the goal was to have it sync individual files even if some were conflicted, right?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07748-5782-7853-a8cd-174e7f0a7cff","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707624.834069,"turn_id":"01a07748-56c2-7e20-b4ff-4dff4121c93a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if we should keep that or have everything move atomically\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07748-c321-7241-80a2-db0910994ff8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707652.385885,"turn_id":"01a07748-c24c-72c1-ad65-85ec7f832d0e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i kind of think \"sync stopped working\" is good since without the notifications users won't know they have conflicts and they're not going to bother with atomic groups\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07749-753f-7742-a6f0-c1bcd9838436","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707697.983667,"turn_id":"01a07749-747e-7080-a0e4-96ca8555a97b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should turn on notifications by default. if we get rid of partial sync does that make things simpler or harder?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774a-485a-7c71-8195-7d2fdd590023","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707752.026807,"turn_id":"01a0774a-478b-7463-8a04-94897d52f450"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774a-fe9c-7d01-8068-b5033e0ee88d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707798.684623,"turn_id":"01a0774a-fdcb-7792-8eb7-c035721bc8dc"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok i want you to take over working on these PRs now. \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774b-677c-7bf2-9038-a448cc9a6cfd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707825.532997,"turn_id":"01a0774b-66c1-7263-b21d-973c6f6715af"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"PLEASE IMPLEMENT THIS PLAN:\n# Take over the dotfiles PR stack\n\n## Summary\n\nTake exclusive ownership of the six existing PRs, finish implementation and review fixes, and deliver a verified, merge-ready stack. The other agent stops pushing. Do not merge the PRs.\n\nPreserve the established design: native-file editing, mise-owned history, bootstrap onboarding, platform variants, and template compatibility.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Whole-setup conflict handling\n\nReplace partial synchronization with this contract:\n\n- Any unresolved conflict pauses shared-branch publication and incoming application for the entire setup.\n- Local checkpoints, fetching, and eligible machine-recovery backups continue.\n- Compute conflicts across the complete eligible setup before publishing or writing incoming files.\n- Keep per-file resolution choices, but record those choices without partially applying the setup. Resume only after all conflicts are resolved.\n- Recompute and validate the plan against current local and remote versions before resuming. A later edit invalidates any resolution based on an older version.\n- Preserve explicit path selection for local rollback; it must not become a way to bypass the global sharing pause.\n\nPreflight the complete incoming batch, including newly declared files and required template sources. Keep protective checkpoints and journaling for mid-write failures. Attempt safe recovery without overwriting concurrent user edits; persist an actionable failure if recovery cannot complete. Describe this as all-or-nothing application, not truly atomic filesystem writes.\n\n### Notifications and health\n\n- Default `history.notify` to true; preserve explicit false settings.\n- Notify once when sharing enters a conflict-paused state. Retries remain silent.\n- Reset notification deduplication after recovery so a later conflict can notify again.\n- Notification failures and headless environments never block operations.\n- Status and doctor report the whole-setup pause, conflicting paths, resolution commands, and last successful application. Local-history and backup health remain distinct.\n\n### Existing review findings\n\nReverify every outstanding finding against current heads; fix valid issues in the earliest owning PR and propagate changes upward.\n\nPrioritize stale pull plans overwriting newer saved edits, missing synchronization baselines for initially identical files, declined-origin state leakage, portable config-directory mapping, and permission-metadata consistency. Validate automated findings rather than accepting them solely because a review tool reported them.\n\nKeep encrypted backups explicitly deferred and rejected when requested; do not silently upload plaintext instead.\n\n## Stack and documentation\n\nMaintain the existing PR order:\n\n1. #12849 — foundation\n2. #12835 — rollback\n3. #12838 — services\n4. #12843 — watcher\n5. #12865 — origin/sync\n6. #12882 — automatic sync/onboarding\n\nUse isolated working branches, preserve unrelated work, and update the existing PR branches. Restack with expected-head checks and force-with-lease only where rebasing requires it; stop if unexpected pushes appear.\n\nUpdate CLI help, generated docs, setup examples, PR descriptions, and the existing blog PR to reflect whole-setup pauses and default-on notifications. Remove claims that unrelated files continue syncing during conflicts. Keep unsupported encryption clearly distinguished from shipped functionality and always lowercase “mise.”\n\n## Verification and completion\n\nAdd or update tests for:\n\n- One conflicted file blocking all shared publication and incoming application while local history, fetching, and eligible backups continue.\n- Resolving multiple conflicts incrementally without partially applying changes.\n- Saved or unsaved edits made after planning never being overwritten by a stale pull.\n- Initially identical machines establishing a baseline and correctly handling subsequent edits.\n- Configuration and referenced sources being validated before application.\n- Mid-application failure, recovery, and concurrent edits.\n- Notification defaults, explicit opt-out, deduplication, and unavailable notifiers.\n- Permission-only changes, selective-save permission isolation, and excluded throttled files.\n- Existing two-machine sync, offline recovery, rollback propagation, platform variants, templates, and local/remote bootstrap workflows.\n\nRun focused tests during development, repository-required lint/render checks before commits, and CI on every updated PR head. Inspect substantive failure logs rather than relying on aggregate status.\n\nReply to review threads with the fix and verification evidence; resolve only findings actually addressed or demonstrated invalid. Finish with all six PRs ready for review, a concise validation report, and explicit remaining limitations. Do not merge.\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774e-73de-7f93-9ac2-a0803ed77c35","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788708025.310217,"turn_id":"01a0774e-7311-7183-bbe0-5d429a7b050b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"use a worktree\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07767-6118-7bd3-b717-4e6e85624eef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788709658.904918,"turn_id":"01a07767-5e9f-7c30-a85f-2921c05466b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok is there feedback on the prs that needs to be addressed?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0776b-d93f-7d41-9f8e-504e2242078c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788709951.807571,"turn_id":"01a0776b-d6fe-7063-9528-850ccb33e91d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok reply to false positives and address feedback, keep checking for feedback, failing checks, and merge conflicts until the entire stack settles\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0776f-8da7-74d3-b917-ecf1c7382bd6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788710194.599302,"turn_id":"01a0776f-8b86-7383-9180-4a703e38ce72"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how does the stack and blog post compare now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077bb-abe7-74c3-89b8-92056406f170","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715183.079516,"turn_id":"01a077bb-ab0c-7253-9092-b7dbbd644e8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Response annotations:\nEach item contains text selected from an earlier Codex response and may include a user comment. Treat items as Annotation 1, Annotation 2, and so on in array order. Use every selection as context and address every comment. For every annotation you address, include its inline directive `:codex-annotation{index=\"N\"}`, where N is its one-based array position (for example, `:codex-annotation{index=\"1\"}`). Do not use unstructured annotation labels.\n\u003cresponse-annotations\u003e\n[{\"text\":\"The blog promises executable configuration requires trust approval. That isn’t fully enforced for synchronized history.describe_command settings. This needs an implementation fix, not just softer wording.\",\"source\":{\"messageId\":\"msg_0749c281f1ff31a6016a9da1059b0487d08d2ef7615898cbcd\",\"startOffset\":564,\"endOffset\":768}}]\n\u003c/response-annotations\u003e\n\n## My request:\nwhat is this?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077be-f5a1-71a1-8df1-09dbb6642280","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715398.561845,"turn_id":"01a077be-f4a5-7821-9ab6-b14af70720cd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is this the claude -p thing?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077bf-cc83-76f1-8526-2281e4a48883","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715453.571856,"turn_id":"01a077bf-cb59-7973-a88e-65cb000207e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is it an escaping problem potentially?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c0-1702-7192-9c2d-7d647bd679bf","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715472.642674,"turn_id":"01a077c0-1625-7b33-8ede-bac0f178de43"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok what should we do?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c0-7063-77a0-8fd6-07e5afc55497","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715495.523049,"turn_id":"01a077c0-6f87-7ab0-b43b-ae4da2f7b2ed"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok add that to one of the prs in the stack\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c1-4815-7332-be85-9750128b9011","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715550.741295,"turn_id":"01a077c1-472f-7723-ad8b-101b0407bd85"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"well is this necessary? if a user is adding a dotfile repo they will be able to get shell execution for sure\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c1-de12-7b73-b385-8365376637f1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715589.138385,"turn_id":"01a077c1-dd3d-7a73-ba44-2d9518554995"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i don't even think it deserves disclosure\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c2-9018-7bc3-bfbc-10703128b387","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715634.712651,"turn_id":"01a077c2-8f37-78d3-a848-062401fb8a21"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok fix the blog post, then let's talk about remote preview, what is it?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c3-084e-7b52-aa78-c9f97c42b651","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715665.486939,"turn_id":"01a077c3-077d-7841-9dc8-8aa22ff57ec9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"explain the other discrepencies and give a proposed solution\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c4-9f31-7412-92ee-9955fe6a0a9c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715769.649301,"turn_id":"01a077c4-9e67-7912-a253-e8ba2cbac16a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how is the stack looking now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07812-c2de-7160-954e-7f53482267a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788720890.590896,"turn_id":"01a07812-c0c9-7891-ab33-63f7eadd24a0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"an agent is working on the encryption pr\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07816-138c-7551-8d60-b8a8db2b3631","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721107.852073,"turn_id":"01a07816-12ae-7601-bfbc-cb79ce8a673b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"no\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07817-59e8-7960-a2d1-cd1b85cb0c54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721191.400247,"turn_id":"01a07817-58e5-7452-b9ae-1628c2fc7906"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what about from a product perspective or tricky parts of this, do you have any questions for me?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07817-b91d-7e20-ad4b-56c8e9e80bcb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721215.773665,"turn_id":"01a07817-b848-7bc1-a012-f7761e8dd7a5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"prompt me for these questions and fix the PRs, leave the encryption one alone \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07819-ad1a-7f33-b25e-f3ded8a99f95","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721343.770661,"turn_id":"01a07819-ac32-7782-a512-d3e0a35b975e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"because this is getting quite complex, tracking should be marked experimental, modify these existing prs to mark it as experimental and gate on ensure_experimental\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0781f-2c0f-70d0-ab95-2df647465a1c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721703.951924,"turn_id":"01a0781f-2b35-7f13-bd06-952e347cb9f8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"be careful with backwards compatibility, this stack will be merged together in the same release and it's been a few days since the last release. be careful no backwards compatibility cruft is in this stack that isn't necessary since no users have this functionality and it will all be shipped together\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07821-e758-7e53-ab6c-912476eecc7f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721882.968288,"turn_id":"01a07821-e65a-79d3-8b70-98cd2b81d2d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-24ab-7833-8602-5037b868e853","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721898.667108,"turn_id":"01a07822-23d7-7c00-a58f-bd5acb0fe8dd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"start building bro\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-8548-7572-99cf-678441d19269","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721923.400499,"turn_id":"01a07822-8479-7bf3-a8d6-b1867ce0cd21"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok go\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-a4b6-7c33-b40d-8c77c0cb3567","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721931.446517,"turn_id":"01a07822-a3e5-7e32-8185-08e4b3a34f79"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what are the blog changes?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07846-621c-76c2-b3bb-60e76aab355c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724273.692029,"turn_id":"01a07846-5f24-7332-8e00-f405474b90b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what did the other agent change?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07849-be29-72d0-a6d1-80a0905ddc84","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724493.865263,"turn_id":"01a07849-bce5-7283-9aba-92d2015f49e5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"push all the changes including yours\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784a-f938-78c3-ac69-be0d9797d083","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724574.520426,"turn_id":"01a0784a-f83d-7222-8d22-de51d10941f7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is there feedback on the stack?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784c-5f1e-7bd2-9b4f-a9a0009f9809","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724666.142911,"turn_id":"01a0784c-5dbd-7f21-b728-2d01af15e259"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"keep addressing feebdack until it settles, feel free to stop if you need clarification\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784e-24d2-7bb2-8560-d5eae3ac2437","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724782.290289,"turn_id":"01a0784e-23cc-77b0-8fe9-f11e1d8bfc76"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"can you add the mise logo to the notifications?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0785f-465f-7310-a873-7ace0e970def","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788725904.991502,"turn_id":"01a0784e-23cc-77b0-8fe9-f11e1d8bfc76"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"keep addressing feebdack until it settles, feel free to stop if you need clarification\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0786f-dbaa-7d32-9396-b6987365648d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788726991.786784,"turn_id":"01a0786f-d930-7653-bdfb-564e4c117620"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_pFiietOWwlygFSZGWAfdn2DZ\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"One rollback edge case needs a product call: Git snapshots don’t record empty directories. Should rolling back a parent directory leave unrecorded empty folders alone, or should we extend history to track empty directories too? I recommend leaving them alone; explicitly selected empty folders can still be removed and restored with undo.\",\"answer\":\"Leave unrecorded empty folders alone\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07882-4b8a-7412-ac9e-67ec16c0a066","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788728200.074042,"turn_id":"01a0786f-d930-7653-bdfb-564e4c117620"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de0e4769c87d0a4cffbe5934cd035","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The foundation, rollback, and services PRs now include the new CLI-reference generator and have passed their render and lint checks locally. I’m carrying that through the watcher and sync PRs before pushing the stack together.\n","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de0e53d1887d0b5d65b6cd1875450","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1788731618.144755,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_bv3RAPVQQa9HOvr2JMgdevqU","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de0e6f73c87d0a5bee252ca3cdcfd","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git restore --ours docs/cli/bootstrap/dotfiles.md docs/cli/index.md \u0026\u0026 git add docs/cli/bootstrap/dotfiles.md docs/cli/index.md \u0026\u0026 GIT_EDITOR=true git rebase --continue\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-watcher/mise\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":1300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788731618.144755,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"name":"exec","status":"compl