elow complete.\\n+\\n+Fourth new fix: #9 rejects unknown top-level keys in incoming whole-file declarations (only incoming validation; released local parser unchanged). Prevents shrae=false silently becoming share=true. New sync_preflight regression PASSED (51405); owning rebased code commit9b5ba2b5e, original4c911682d. Needs reply/resolve3945310318 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ after push. Variant fix nowbbecdbe4c; rollback fix5399cb731; purge fix4281da00d. Other three new findings need replies after push as below. Still no GitHub replies this heartbeat.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732082.210153,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_QyB2NHfP3SGDrfRh4ZOYnY2d","id":"ctco_01a078bd-ecaf-7de0-ab32-06a762dc9f5f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732107.951332,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":[{"text":"the agenti had working on the encryption prs is done so you should include that now in these checks\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078bd-ed73-7143-ad39-8b7d6042e80b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788732108.147861,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2d1a2c087d0896eb287fb42c35d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Got it—I’ll include the encryption PRs in the review and CI checks now. I’ll first identify their branches and current heads so I can preserve the other agent’s finished work when restacking.\n","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2d5df8c87d08fce4a01c4ce5999","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1788732110.95112,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_meEGyJCd9OEgiV32ecCzu3DY","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2d721b487d085eba479e5ecec9e","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr list --repo jdx/mise --state open --limit 100 --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,url --jq '.[] | select((.title|ascii_downcase|contains(\\\"encrypt\\\")) or (.headRefName|ascii_downcase|contains(\\\"encrypt\\\")))'\",\"max_output_tokens\":1800}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:57064,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\ntext(ALL_TOOLS.filter(x=\u003e/automation_update/.test(x.name)));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732110.95112,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_meEGyJCd9OEgiV32ecCzu3DY","id":"ctco_01a078be-3848-7b20-9d10-c6b6eae1fc88","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732127.304656,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ea7b12\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.239023084,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":55,\"output\":\"{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"bootstrap/10-auto-sync\\\",\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups\\\",\\\"number\\\":12895,\\\"title\\\":\\\"feat(dotfiles): encrypt shared files and machine backups\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/jdx/mise/pull/12895\\\"}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"495f87\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.002035167,\"session_id\":57064,\"original_token_count\":383,\"output\":\"mise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\n[docs:setup] $ bun i\\n[docs:setup] bun install v1.4.0 (34cbb9a40)\\n[docs:setup] \\n[docs:setup] Checked 269 installs across 331 packages (no changes) [71.00ms]\\n[docs:setup] Finished in 81.2ms\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\n[render:schema] $ ~/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-auto/mise/xtasks/render/schema.ts\\n[render:schema] schema/mise.json 46ms\\n[render:schema] schema/mise-task.json 6ms\\n[render:schema] schema/miserc.json 1ms (unchanged)\\n[render:schema] Finished in 183.5ms\\n[build]    Compiling mise-interactive-config v2026.1.12 (/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-auto/mise/crates/mise-interactive-config)\\n[build]    Compiling mise v2026.9.1 (/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-auto/mise)\\n[build] mbx[warning]: incremental state was not reused: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\n[build] mbx[warning]: prediction was not restored: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"[{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_app__automation_update\",\"description\":\"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nCreate, update, view, or delete recurring automations in the Codex app. The automation prompt is user-visible and is replayed by the scheduler. Write clear, cohesive, human-readable prose. Use this when the user asks for a scheduled task, automation, recurring run, repeated task, reminder, follow-up, monitor, or asks you to watch something, keep an eye on it, check back later, wake up later, notify them, or keep working later. Heartbeat automations are proactive follow-ups attached to the current local thread and are the default for recurring requests. Use a heartbeat unless the user explicitly asks for a new task per run or standalone project work. Cron automations run as standalone local jobs against one project; use list_projects to find its project id. Never write raw automation directives by hand, show raw RRULE strings to the user, or create a workaround cron automation for a thread heartbeat unless the user explicitly asks for that. For requests about existing automations, inspect $CODEX_HOME/automations/*/automation.toml to find matching automation ids by name or prompt. Prefer updating an existing automation over creating a duplicate. For updates, preserve existing fields unless the user asks to change them, and call automation_update with the resolved id and full updated fields. Treat requests such as 'don't notify me' or 'mute this automation' as notificationPolicy=failed_runs_only, and set notificationPolicy=null when the user asks to unmute. Keep notification preferences out of the automation prompt.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_app__automation_update(args: { id: string; mode: \\\"view\\\"; } | { destination?: \\\"local\\\"; executionEnvironment: \\\"local\\\"; kind: \\\"cron\\\"; mode: \\\"create\\\" | \\\"suggested_create\\\"; model: string; name: string; notificationPolicy?: \\\"failed_runs_only\\\" | null; projectId: string | null; prompt: string; reasoningEffort: \\\"none\\\" | \\\"minimal\\\" | \\\"low\\\" | \\\"medium\\\" | \\\"high\\\" | \\\"xhigh\\\" | \\\"max\\\" | \\\"ultra\\\"; rrule: string; status: \\\"ACTIVE\\\" | \\\"PAUSED\\\"; } | { destination?: \\\"local\\\" | \\\"thread\\\"; kind: \\\"heartbeat\\\"; mode: \\\"create\\\" | \\\"suggested_create\\\"; name: string; notificationPolicy?: \\\"failed_runs_only\\\" | null; prompt: string; rrule: unknown; status: unknown; targetThreadId?: unknown; } | unknown | unknown): Promise\u003cCallToolResult\u003e; };\\n```\"}]","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2e234e087d089ba2fb542ad2702","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_GCEmqnnu4JUQWyW6NqE91UgE","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2e38c2c87d0b4192c4b2e1cce38","input":"text(await tools.mcp__codex_app__automation_update({id:\"settle-dotfiles-pr-stack\",mode:\"view\"}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr view 12895 --repo jdx/mise --json title,headRefOid,baseRefOid,headRefName,baseRefName,body,mergeable,statusCheckRollup --jq '{title,headRefOid,baseRefOid,headRefName,baseRefName,body,mergeable,failed:[.statusCheckRollup[]|select(.conclusion==\\\"FAILURE\\\")|{name,detailsUrl}],pending:[.statusCheckRollup[]|select(.status==\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\" or .status==\\\"QUEUED\\\")|.name]}'\",\"max_output_tokens\":3500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732127.793409,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_GCEmqnnu4JUQWyW6NqE91UgE","id":"ctco_01a078be-5cbf-7cb0-84f4-95c1bf163a16","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732136.639576,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Rendered automation card in the app.\"}],\"isError\":false}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"bc29db\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.418224458,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1399,\"output\":\"{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"bootstrap/10-auto-sync\\\",\\\"baseRefOid\\\":\\\"5cb5808be0e2a8c42667cbf47b854a19dc26fcc0\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Stacked on #12882 (`bootstrap/10-auto-sync`). Adds age encryption for selected synced dotfiles and machine recovery backups, including user-installed hardware identity plugins.\\\\n\\\\n## Behavior\\\\n\\\\n```toml\\\\n[history.encryption]\\\\nrecipients = [\\\\\\\"\\\\u003cmac-public-recipient\\\\u003e\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"\\\\u003clinux-public-recipient\\\\u003e\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"\\\\u003crecovery-public-recipient\\\\u003e\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n[dotfiles]\\\\n\\\\\\\"~/.config/app/credentials\\\\\\\" = { mode = \\\\\\\"track\\\\\\\", encrypt = true }\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nOne shared recipient list protects tracked contents and external copy, symlink, and template sources. Each consumer decrypts with its own matching identity. Publication writes versioned envelopes at existing logical paths, binds their contents to the path and original mode, and upgrades the setup marker to format 2. Existing format-1 repositories remain readable; older clients reject format 2.\\\\n\\\\nReconciliation and conflict decisions use local plaintext objects. Ciphertext is reused when content, mode, and recipients are unchanged. Recipient changes re-encrypt current protected files in one leased branch update. Missing decryption access pauses application and publication for the entire setup; fetching and local history continue. Invalid encryption declarations and overlapping plaintext/encrypted sources fail closed. Inline secrets must move to external sources.\\\\n\\\\n`origin set --encrypt-backups [--recipient …]` configures separate, machine-local backup recipients. Defaults use available age/SSH public keys or generate an age identity. Encrypted files are excluded from plaintext remote backups, including rebuilt historical checkpoints. Encrypted backups can include them under that machine's backup recipients.\\\\n\\\\nUser-installed age plugins support Secure Enclave and TPM identities through existing identity settings. Both legacy plugin recipients and native `age1tag` TPM recipients work. Software and hardware recipients can be mixed; hardware-only configurations warn about device loss. Only locally configured identities select plugins. Background work never launches hardware identity plugins, and diagnostics report hardware restorability as configured but unverified. Interactive pull and rollback can request authorization.\\\\n\\\\nPaths, configuration, and recipient public keys remain visible on the shared branch. Live files, rendered outputs, local history, and decrypted caches remain plaintext. Enabling encryption or removing recipients cannot erase earlier Git history or copies already held by other consumers.\\\\n\\\\n## Backup review fixes\\\\n\\\\n- Select the requested checkpoint before decrypting it; unreadable siblings cannot block an unscoped restore.\\\\n- Build all replacement wrappers before one atomic push of updates and deletions. Unsupported servers retain existing refs. Record migration success only after publication; interrupted retries remain safe.\\\\n- Preserve previously uploaded, locally retained eligible history when changing schemes or recipients without `--include-existing`.\\\\n- Validate remote namespace, header, and payload identity before materialization or cached reuse.\\\\n- Probe software restorability using actual age decryption, including SSH recipients. Preserve encrypted status when the local origin declaration is missing.\\\\n- Keep ordinary plaintext files outside the encrypted-envelope size cap and skip submodule commits during envelope detection; schema validation rejects encrypted inline declarations while preserving `encrypt = false`. Accept SHA-1 and SHA-256 gitlink IDs, and restore test environment values with scoped guards.\\\\n- Bound encrypted/compressed input to 256 MiB, decoded input to 1 GiB, and backups to 100,000 files. Validate paths, duplicates, ancestor collisions, and modes before Git writes. Non-UTF-8 paths fail explicitly rather than being silently renamed.\\\\n\\\\n## Validation\\\\n\\\\nFocused history, age, settings, and doctor unit tests; encrypted-file and backup e2e tests plus adjacent sync, watcher, onboarding, rollback, and age environment tests. Regression coverage includes two independent consumers, copy/template/symlink sources, executable modes, deletion, conflict resolution, recipient rotation, no-churn sync, missing keys, malformed settings, atomic-push failure/retry, damaged sibling checkpoints, and scans of published Git objects for protected plaintext.\\\\n\\\\nProtocol fixtures cover hardware/software recipients, native TPM recipient encryption, missing plugins, cancelled authorization, noninteractive refusal, and software recovery. **Real Secure Enclave/TPM hardware has not been exercised.**\\\\n\\\\nSchema, CLI usage/man page, and documentation are updated. The accompanying announcement is updated in jdx/blog#99. Final local checks pass: 66 history tests, 13 age tests, 74 settings tests, 3 doctor tests, the encrypted-file/backup and adjacent e2e coverage, Clippy (`--workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`), the no-default-features check with CI's vendored-Lua feature selection and `RUSTFLAGS=-D unused`, formatting, and scoped safe hk fixes. The plain-sync regression also passes. Build/test CI was explicitly dispatched for commit `111476665`: [workflow run](https://github.com/jdx/mise/actions/runs/34059651602).\\\\n\\\\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\\\\n\\\",\\\"failed\\\":[],\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"11147666527317c2cfcb389f261a64922548976c\\\",\\\"mergeable\\\":\\\"UNKNOWN\\\",\\\"pending\\\":[],\\\"title\\\":\\\"feat(dotfiles): encrypt shared files and machine backups\\\"}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2ec726887d097121ea9a6bf4e86","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_ZN75WDpbXZympVGIuk13uiN6","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9de2f4348487d0906782b7f8df3340","input":"text(await tools.mcp__codex_app__automation_update({mode:\"update\",id:\"settle-dotfiles-pr-stack\",kind:\"heartbeat\",name:\"Settle dotfiles PR stack\",status:\"ACTIVE\",rrule:\"FREQ=MINUTELY;INTERVAL=30\",targetThreadId:\"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb\",prompt:\"Continue settling jdx/mise PRs #12849, #12835, #12838, #12843, #12865, #12882, and #12895 (encryption). The encryption agent has finished; include its completed work in review, CI, integration, and restacking checks. Use isolated worktrees and preserve local changes. Read the latest handoff in /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md. Check new review feedback, substantive failing CI logs, and merge conflicts. Validate findings, fix valid issues in their earliest owning PR, restack safely with expected-head checks, reply with verification evidence and resolve only addressed or invalid findings. Preserve experimental tracking gates and released backward compatibility without compatibility scaffolding for unreleased stack revisions. Preserve the encryption implementation and never silently substitute plaintext. Never merge. Stop on unexpected remote pushes or required product clarification and request direction. Stay quiet when unchanged; notify only on actionable changes, blockers, or when all seven PRs are verified and ready for review. Pause this automation once the stack is settled.\"}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git worktree list --porcelain; gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:\\\"jdx\\\",name:\\\"mise\\\") { pullRequest(number:12895) { reviewThreads(last:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(first:1) { nodes { databaseId body } } } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved|not)|{id,comment:.comments.nodes[0].databaseId,body:(.comments.nodes[0].body|gsub(\\\"\u003cdetails\u003e[\\\\\\\\s\\\\\\\\S]*?\u003c/details\u003e\\\";\\\"\\\")|.[0:1700])}'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-auto/mise\",\"max_output_tokens\":2800}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732137.126058,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_ZN75WDpbXZympVGIuk13uiN6","id":"ctco_01a078be-bc22-72a0-9766-ee1ae001b796","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788732161.058791,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Updated automation in the app.\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"automationId\\\":\\\"settle-dotfiles-pr-stack\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"update\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"ACTIVE\\\"}\"}],\"isError\":false}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f09731\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.237963166,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1155,\"output\":\"worktree /Users/jdx/src/mise\\nHEAD 772faebf1252afffd6f1a8a6ce08d13c0c91ccfe\\nbranch refs/heads/codex/fix-vfox-lockfile-tool-name\\n\\nworktree /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jdx-src-packslip--claude-worktrees-local-cloudflare-browser-a49dcf/cc4eaa14-bf7b-42f6-a18e-791d094ed9bc/scratchpad/mise-main\\nHEAD b8e5f1594cfbb6a145416c5ec0678adf1479d701\\ndetached\\n\\nworktree /private/tmp/codex-ai-review-release-prs/mise\\nHEAD 308b8744e6f60c91716fd6b4193812dab0c0e12b\\nbranch refs/heads/codex/skip-ai-release-pr-reviews-20260709\\nprunable gitdir file points to non-existent location\\n\\nworktree /private/tmp/mise-docs-toml11\\nHEAD 4c58ee3ef298e6ec68e761145fb6ab607fb8bd96\\nbranch refs/heads/codex/docs-restore-toml11\\n\\nworktree /private/tmp/mise-github-attestations-option\\nHEAD 30b1aa7f76f34a0b22af1d9c905fe5959ee123e8\\nbranch refs/heads/codex/github-attestations-tool-option\\nprunable gitdir file points to non-existent location